On Wed, Jul 20, 2005 at 08:15:21AM -0500, Chris Capel wrote:
> So http://lojban.org is not running Tiki yet? 

That's correct.

> We're commenting just on the design of wiki.lojban.org?

Yes.

> That "toolbar" thing at the top (with the 3d button and print and
> export to pdf and such) is superfluous to the vast majority of
> visitors. 

True.  I'll see about moving that to the bottom.

> The left side containing all the toolbars should be in a
> font at least one size smaller (like, small or x-small instead of
> medium). 

There are *no* size directives in either the CSS or the HTML.  I'd
prefer to leave that up to the individual use; on my display, the
menu text is already about as small as I'm comfortable with.

Having said all that, however, I suppose I might as well play with
it.  Is there a way in CSS to say "render this one size smaller than
the default"?

> In the default color scheme, the blue headers of the bars draw way
> too much attention to them, when the attention should be first
> drawn to the content in the center. The toolbar headers need to be
> much lower contrast, or there should be a different background or
> border around the main body to make it draw the eye.

Broca's been the one doing that sort of thing, so I'll let him take
a crack at it.

